        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1678423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-14T23:27:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Gil! This is very useful feedback. I have updated the documentation to specify the requirements w.r.t the \"use after destroy\" threat and an example approach of addressing such requirements with the global sequence number.\n\nRe: \n\u003e maybe some platforms have transport ids that are not reusable so they can trust the hypervisor to prevent use-after-destroy threats\nI am not sure about the transport id -  AFAIK, it is per pVM boot, in which case we cannot use it for storage related things. But I am not sure if this is the case for all the platforms.",
      "parentUuid": "e84f0b31_99cd29a6",
      "revId": "203736ffee832d58e85fd9fa67298a6bc42de47b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
